0","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-uv.1","local_name":"sase-uv.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-uv","agent_clan_generation":"20260827122834","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-uv.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-uv[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Restore ACE TUI responsiveness[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Pressing a key in `sase ace` never blocks on provider discovery, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]git subprocesses, or filesystem walks; the steady-state agent [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]refresh costs a fraction of today's ~800 ms warm / 2-3 s loaded [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]full rebuild; and both are held there by benches that fail when the[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]budgets regress.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]9[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]ace_tui_responsiveness.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fresh perf baseline and durable budget benches[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]baseline[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]baseline: capture a current-master keystroke and loader baseline, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add the benches that assert the epic's budgets so later phases have a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pass/fail gate.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Take provider discovery off the keystroke path[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]keypath[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]keypath: make accent/icon resolution for fixed panes table-driven, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]memoize fixed descriptors, and convert resolve_artifacts_subtabs to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]serve-stale-revalidate-in-background so no keystroke can fork git.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Collapse the redundant link-subject resolutions per keystroke[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]railcalls[dim] · [dim][/dim]after keypath[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]railcalls: cache the resolved LinkSubject per selection and coalesce the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]three call sites so one j/k costs at most one subject resolution instead[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]of three.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make the artifact delta the default refresh, not the 2% [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]exception[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]delta[dim] · [dim][/dim]after baseline[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]delta: replace the all-or-nothing watcher-path classification with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]partial application so an unmapped path no longer discards the whole [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]queued batch and escalates to a full reload.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Remove the per-workflow-step filesystem enrichment from every [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]load[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]stepmeta[dim] · [dim][/dim]after baseline[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]stepmeta: eliminate the 1,532 per-load enrich_agent_from_meta filesystem[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]calls the workflow-step builder makes, the single largest Python cost in[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the loader.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Drop the double tree build in the artifact-index PyO3 binding[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]marshal[dim] · [dim][/dim]after baseline[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]marshal: serialize the query snapshot straight into Python objects [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instead of building an intermediate serde_json::Value tree, halving the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]GIL-held marshalling.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Project the heavy record_json leaves off the list-render path[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]projection[dim] · [dim][/dim]after marshal[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]projection: add a list-shaped record projection in sase-core that omits [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the four leaf fields making up 78% of the payload, and hydrate them [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lazily for the selected row.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Honour the AgentsViewport contract instead of discarding it[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]viewport[dim] · [dim][/dim]after projection, delta, stepmeta[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]viewport: wire the bounded read window through DirectAgentsDataProvider [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]so a refresh stops building 430 agents to paint 12 rows; [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]measurement-gated on whether the earlier phases already met budget.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Index retention tooling and self-inflicted stall fixes[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]hygiene[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]hygiene: add retention/vacuum tooling for the unbounded index and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]registry state, open the index read-only on query paths, and stop the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stall watchdog from extending the freeze it measures.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-uv","llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-uv.1","reasoning_e